From 65f5b67940a79dcbf15e72389bcceb2ed263de72 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: rkvenc forward-port <forward-port@local>
Date: Sat, 8 Aug 2026 12:51:06 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 94/94] video: rockchip: rga3: stage incompatible RGA2 DMA-BUFs

Prefer RGA3 for high DMA-BUF jobs when it is compatible. For RGA2-only work whose exporter SG entry exceeds the SWIOTLB mapping ceiling, copy CPU-accessible buffers through a bounded job-owned DMA32 staging object. Share staging across aliased planes and tasks, copy output back only after successful quiesced completion, and expose lifecycle counters in debugfs.
